# a-plate-on-the-approach — BACKLOG C4, and the trip is the mechanic.
#
# ⚠⚠ **This is `a-base-that-plays-its-list.keys` with a PLATE on the hex
# in front of the gate, and a second pair of hands.**  Same ground, same
# wall with the same opening at (6, 0), same towers, same four-wave
# list, same poke.  What is added is one trap marker at (7, 0) — and an
# errand: when the plate has gone off, somebody has to go out and
# re-arm it.
#
# ⚠ **A plate fires ONCE** (`@X108`).  It kills what walks onto it and
# everything within one hex, and then it is a dead plate in the ground
# until a vehicle stands on it for twenty seconds.  Nothing in this file
# presses a key to re-arm it: re-arming is a POSITION, the same as
# clearing rubble and rebuilding a tower.
#
# ⚠⚠ **The way out is the gate the wave is coming through**, which is
# the whole cost.  The errand below is run in the LULL, after wave 1 has
# been cleared and before wave 2 arrives, because that is the only
# window it fits in — and it takes TWO crew members, because one alone
# does not finish twenty seconds of work before the next wave is on top
# of them.  Measured, on this base's cousin: sent out mid-wave, a lone
# crew member is destroyed at (7, 0) after about twenty ticks with the
# plate still dead.
#
# ⚠ `tests/c4_the_trap.loft` § One hex decides the trip is the
# controlled version: a plate at (7, 0) re-armed three times is worth
# **+106 ticks**, the same plate left spent is worth **−3**, and one hex
# further out the crew never gets through its own gate at all.

echo a plate on the approach: it fires once, and somebody has to go and re-arm it

do toggle_mode

do cycle_kind
click 0 0
marker 0 0 target

do cycle_kind
click 1 0
click 1 2
click 1 -2
marker 1 0 tower
marker 1 2 tower

# ⚠ The fourth marker kind (BACKLOG C4).  The editor cycles
# spawn → target → tower → trap, so a plate is one more press — and
# every `.keys` file in the corpus grew that press when this kind
# landed, which is what `CLAUDE.md` § Add a marker kind warns about.
do cycle_kind
click 7 0
marker 7 0 trap

do cycle_kind
do rotate
do rotate
do rotate
click 18 0
marker 18 0 spawn 3

count markers 6 6
do toggle_mode

palette 5
drag -3 -2 20 -2
drag -3 -1 20 -1
drag -3 0 20 0
drag -3 1 20 1
drag -3 2 20 2
count painted 120 120

# The wall, with (6, 0) left open — and the plate is the hex in FRONT
# of the opening, where the column funnels.
palette 9
click 6 -2
click 6 -1
click 6 1
click 6 2
kind 6 0 grass
kind 6 1 wall

# Two crew members beside the core.  They are the errand.
crew 0 1
crew 0 -1
helper 0 0 1
helper 1 0 -1
roster 2 2
park 0 0

schedule 12 12 12 12
waves 0 0
count alive 0 0

# ⚠ A plate nobody has set off is ARMED, and the run holds no cell of
# state for it at all — `trap.loft` § The field stores SPENT.
armed 7 0 on

# ── The poke ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
drive 18 0
tick 10
vehicle 18 0
waves 1 1
count alive 12 12

# ── The drive home, in front of them ────────────────────────────
drive 0 0
tick 10
vehicle 0 0

# ── ⚠ The plate goes off under the first thing that reaches it ──
#
# Nothing here fires it.  Twelve robots walk the road, the leading one
# steps onto (7, 0), and the charge takes it and everything within a
# hex of it.
tick 30
armed 7 0 off
count alive 0 0
pile 7 0 0.5 0.5

# ── ⚠⚠ The errand, run in the lull ──────────────────────────────
#
# Out through the gate in two legs, because a vehicle drives in a
# straight line and the wall is in the way of the first one.
send 0 6 0
send 1 6 0
tick 12
helper 0 6 0
helper 1 6 0

send 0 7 0
send 1 8 0
tick 6
helper 0 7 0
helper 1 8 0

# ⚠ **Sixteen ticks, not thirty**, and that is `wave_rearm`'s *any
# number of vehicles per plate*: one crew member stands ON the plate
# and the other one hex from it, so the twenty seconds are paid twice
# over at once.  It is also why one alone does not make it.
tick 16
armed 7 0 on
roster 2 2

# ── And home again, before wave 2 is on them ────────────────────
send 0 6 0
send 1 6 0
tick 8
send 0 0 1
send 1 0 -1
tick 14
helper 0 0 1
helper 1 0 -1
roster 2 2

# ── ⚠ And it fires a SECOND time, unattended ────────────────────
#
# The plate is live again and nobody is near it.  Wave 2 walks down the
# same road onto the same hex.
tick 60
armed 7 0 off

# ── The rest of the list, and what the base came to ─────────────
#
# ⚠ Both crew members come home: the errand was survivable because it
# was run in the lull, which is the only thing this file does that
# `a-base-that-plays-its-list.keys` does not.
tick 500
waves 4 4
count alive 0 0
roster 2 2
wallet 393.0 394.0

snap c4_a_plate_on_the_approach
